CORE
JmlBasic
--function JmlBasic.identity --jml-source src/main/java/JmlBasic.java --unwind 5 -cp target/classes --static-coverage
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^Proof explanation:$
^Per-property proof explanations:$
^Static coverage: every contract element contributes to a property's proof\.$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
^Static coverage warnings:$
--
Phase 4 regression test for --static-coverage on JBMC.

Reuses the JmlBasic.identity test class with
`//@ requires x >= 0; //@ ensures \\result >= x;`. The precondition
and the postcondition are both used in the proof, so this is the
"all elements contribute" positive case: the static-coverage
report should print the "every contract element contributes"
acknowledgement and emit no per-element warnings.

Verifies:
- --static-coverage implies --proof-explanation (both section
  headers appear).
- The "Static coverage:" acknowledgement line is printed.
- No "Static coverage warnings:" header is printed.

This pairs with the unit tests in
unit/goto-checker/proof_explanation/classify_uncovered.cpp which
exercise classify_uncovered() directly — those cover the per-
element warning kinds (UNNECESSARY_PRECONDITION, etc.) without
needing an unsat-core-capable solver wired in at the CLI level.
